{
  "id": "mixed-effects-model",
  "term": "mixed-effects model",
  "definition": "A mixed-effects model is a statistical approach for repeated or longitudinal data that estimates both overall patterns in a population and differences in change within individual subjects over time. It is commonly used when the same people are measured at multiple time points, especially when trajectories may vary across individuals.",
